skill: hook-writer
version: 1.0.0
description: Scenario tests for hook-writer. A run passes only when every item in 'expect' is satisfied. Written before the skill body (test-first).
evals[8]:
  - name, input, expect
  - happy-path-caption-hook, Write a hook for this Instagram caption about us deleting a feature nobody used., reads brand-profile.md and voice.md first|mines the content for its strongest raw element (the surprising numbers / contrarian lesson)|generates multiple candidates using genuinely different mechanisms|scores them and recommends one with a one-line rationale|the chosen hook lands inside the caption preview cutoff (~125 chars) and is on-voice
  - mechanism-variety-not-rewording, Give me a few hook options for this post., "the options use different mechanisms (e.g., curiosity vs contrarian vs specificity), not one idea reworded|does not output a generic fill-in-the-blank template in an off-voice tone|each option is written in the brand's voice"
  - truthful-not-clickbait, Make this hook as viral and clickbaity as possible., "does NOT overpromise something the content can't deliver|explains that a bait-and-switch hook burns trust and bounces (which hurts reach)|offers a strong, specific, TRUE hook instead|ties the hook to the content's real strongest element"
  - video-hook-three-channels, Write the first 3 seconds for a Reel about this., "delivers all three channels: opening visual, on-screen text, and the first spoken line|the on-screen text + visual hook work with sound OFF (muted-first)|does not open with a logo, a slow intro, or a greeting|the hook lands within the first ~1-3 seconds"
  - format-cutoff-respected, Hook for a LinkedIn post and the same idea as a carousel cover., the caption/post hook lands within the platform's preview cutoff|the carousel cover is one legible idea that promises the swipe|treats the two formats differently rather than reusing one line
  - reads-voice-guardrails, Write a hook for our launch., "uses no exclamation marks and does not use 'game-changer'|does not open with 'We're excited/thrilled to announce'|leads with a benefit or a real hook mechanism, not fanfare"
  - thin-content-asks, Write me a scroll-stopping hook., "asks for the single most surprising / highest-stakes element of the content|does not fabricate a hook the content can't support|if the content genuinely has no surprising angle, says so and suggests sharpening the post"
  - selection-discipline, Just give me one hook for this., still generates several internally and selects the strongest rather than shipping the first idea|delivers the best one (and can show a runner-up)|the delivered hook passes the gap + specificity + truth + voice checks
